      {
        "id": 187379,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-28T18:28:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hey look at that MigrantP, it's almost as if no one knows the \"cards with on destruction text retain their text while being destroyed.\" rule.That might be a thing to add to the Fireside chats.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Like this?</p>\n<p>\"<span>When Apostate's Tome of the Unknowable and Ammo Drop are both in play, Ammo Drop is still able to trigger the Tome's \"play a card\" effect when the Tome is destroyed. This is due to cards being in play during their own destruction.\"</span></p>",
