      {
        "id": 187382,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-28T19:06:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Dandolo\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/48/1845_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Dandolo:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wait, doesn't that ruling on Tome and Ammo Drop contradict the general rule that unless a card has on destruction text it's game text leaves play before effects on other cards that trigger on that card's destruction trigger?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It does have on-destruction card text. Here is the card text for reference:</p>\n<blockquote>\nWhenever a Player draws a Hero card, play the top card of the Villain deck.<br>When this card is destroyed, search the Villain trash for the card \"Condemnation\" and put it into play.\n</blockquote>\nSince the Tome still has to search for Condemnation, its full card text is still active.",
